            "original": "The average grain diameter was calculated to be 59.9 μm in LSHR when excluding twin boundaries. The final volume fraction measurements between the two alloys fall within the measurement error. Secondary γ′ VF = 43.52 ± 1.7%, tertiary γ′ VF = 2.27 ± 0.1%, total γ′ VF = 45.80 ± 1.8%. Average secondary γ′ size = 154 nm, average tertiary γ′ size = 15.9 nm. Tertiary γ particles present inside the γ′ precipitates. Along SISFs: Co and W segregation with Cr segregation; Ni and Al depletion; Co₃W χ phase (D0₁₉) confirmed by HAADF-STEM simulation. Along SESFs: Co, Cr, Nb, Mo, Ti, and W segregation; Al and Ni depletion; η phase formation observed on some sections. Microtwin: 6 atomic layer thick microtwin observed inside γ′ precipitate; γ phase segregation (Co, Cr, Mo rich; Ni, Al, Ti depleted) with W segregated to twin interfaces.",
